# Rewrites that keep every bit: a transpose feeding a product is never
# materialized (`matmul[ta]`), a matrix times its own transpose computes one
# triangle (`alg=syrk`, and the result is Symmetric, so its transpose is
# itself), and a Diagonal matrix scales rows or columns.
A: Matrix[40, 30]
B: Matrix[40, 20]
D: Diagonal Matrix[40, 40]
E: Diagonal Matrix[20, 20]
x = Aᵀ @ B
gram = Aᵀ @ A
outer = A @ Aᵀ
same = transpose(gram)
rows = D @ B
cols = B @ E
print(x, gram, outer, same, rows, cols)
